#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:61
#: 
msgid "GPS Failsafe and Glitch Protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:5
#: 99d09404cc314a1da481f48a86d6c7a3
msgid "EKF Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:7
#: fb0fc0314cb542809ec56529d785470f
msgid "The EKF failsafe monitors the health of EKF (the position and attitude estimation system) to catch problems with the vehicle's position estimate (often caused by GPS glitches or compass errors) and prevent \"flyaways\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:10
#: e1dd309f7e0749f2a860fd0fa6de553e
msgid "When will it trigger?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:12
#: a318a8ab8f994e7db1eb7a6a732d73e3
msgid "The EKF failsafe will trigger when any two of the EKF \"variances\" for compass, position or velocity are higher than the :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` parameter value for 1 second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:14
#: 33b15e1b4889442a8e5298b4d00b2b0e
msgid "These \"variances\" come from the EKF itself and are numbers indicating the EKF's confidence in its estimates.  The values are between 0 and 1 with 0 meaning the estimate is very trustworthy and 1.0 is very untrustworthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:16
#: 600f5682e2434ab292613a5aaff838e7
msgid "The EKF calculates these \"variances\" by comparing the results from multiple sensors.  So for example, if the GPS position suddenly jumps but the accelerometers do not show a sudden acceleration, the EKF variance for position would climb (i.e become less trustworthy)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:18
#: 8106cf2355684f2cb3e62cf461b2d847
msgid "The variances can be viewed in real-time on the ground station.  If using Mission Planner click on the \"EKF\" label on the HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:25
#: db0b5ee89cbf4f04ab191ca8cbaab334
msgid "What will happen when the failsafe triggers?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:27
#: 23be5b2e6e2844da9c20547ca772031d
msgid "The autopilot's `LED will flash red-yellow or blue-yellow and the tone-alarm will sound <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j-CMLrAwlco&feature=player_detailpage&t=60s>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:28
#: 2a5e17bfa3c442fa92439e53c3d08f13
msgid "\"EKF variance\" will appear on the ground station's HUD if telemetry is connected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:29
#: 32c06a77101e496085e8f28c9e072188
msgid "In manual flight modes that do not require GPS (i.e. Stabilize, Acro, AltHold) nothing further will happen but the pilot will be unable to switch into autonomous flight modes (Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Guided, Auto) until the failure clears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:30
#: ec479cfef75f4fbfad39d5396191b39d
msgid "In autonomous modes that require GPS (i.e. Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Guided, Auto, etc) the :ref:`FS_EKF_ACTION <FS_EKF_ACTION>` controls the behaviour.  By default this is \"1\" meaning the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode.  This is a \"pilot controlled\" land meaning the pilot will have control of the roll and pitch angle but the vehicle will descend at the :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS <LAND_SPD_MS>`.  It will land and finally disarm its motors. Other options are to report only (\"0\"), hover (ALTHOLD) (\"2\") or LAND (\"3\") even if in STABILIZE mode if the EKF failsafe occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:31
#: 7636ec3ea80a42b5adcbb69314eb848e
msgid "An EKF failsafe error will be written to the dataflash logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:33
#: df8ae659a13e4db88dcd042153715783
msgid "After an EKF failsafe occurs, the pilot can re-take control (using the flight mode switch) in a manual flight mode such as :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` to bring the vehicle home."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:36
#: 4183f9508b9348bf8758b1e8222b1442
msgid "Adjusting the Sensitivity of the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:38
#: 6976f2c4e27d45aab62b38255a846ec0
msgid "The :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` parameter can be adjusted to control the sensitivity of the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:40
#: 7e1edf4860a34e7b92f1fb7d48c0213a
msgid "Set :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` = 0 to disable the EKF failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:41
#: 9c5b7a44e0934554a380cb5aa4575df3
msgid "Increase :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` to values between 0.8 and 1.0 to reduce the chance of an EKF failsafe.  The downside of increasing this parameter value is that during a flyaway caused by a bad compass or GPS glitch, the vehicle will fly further away before the vehicle is automatically switched to LAND mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:42
#: 594284ac3e0f4d94b69e2a63e1fac820
msgid "Decrease :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` to values as low as 0.6 to increase the chance of an EKF failsafe triggering quickly.  The downside of lowering this value is the EKF failsafe could trigger a LAND during aggressive maneuvers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:45
#: ac95a8c4061a407ca439b16601fac581
msgid "Dataflash Log example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:47
#: 8bbb0791a5024fab82394ff536815231
msgid "The EKF's innovations can be viewed by graphing a dataflash log's NKF4.SP (position innovation), NKF4.SV (velocity innovation) and NKF4.SM (compass innovation) values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:49
#: 9628a2a7e0a5454e95d7247bfe6cfedf
msgid "The graph below show the EKF's innovations for position (green), velocity (red) and compass (yellow) during an actual EKF failsafe event.  During this incident external interference (probably from a high-powered radio tower nearby) caused the GPS to report inaccurate positions and velocities.  The vehicle switches to Land mode soon after both velocity and position innovations climb over the :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH<FS_EKF_THRESH>` value of 0.8"
msgstr ""

